[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=2]
\draw[-{Stealth}] (-1.3,0)--(1.3,0) node[right,font=\scriptsize]{$x$};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,-1.3)--(0,1.3) node[above,font=\scriptsize]{$y$};
\draw (0,0) circle (1);
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (210:1);
\draw[thick,blue] (O)--(P);
\draw (0.32,0) arc (0:210:0.32);
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (105:0.55) {$210^{\circ}$};
\fill[red] (P) circle (1.2pt);
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (P) {$P$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The radius to $P$ makes an angle of $210^{\circ}$ with the positive $x$-axis.
Which coordinate of $P$ gives $\sin\theta$, and is $\sin\theta$ positive or negative?

